import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Engineering & Standards Disclaimer — HowNote"
  description="Important limitations for HowNote calculations, standards references and sourcing information."
>
  <section class="hero container legal-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Disclaimer</div>
    <h1>Know what a HowNote result does—and does not—mean.</h1>
    <p>Last updated: August 21, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <article class="container prose">
    <h2>Calculated values are estimates</h2>
    <p>Pipe weight results are theoretical values calculated from geometry and an entered density. Actual product weight can differ because of dimensional tolerances, material composition, coating, manufacturing variation, end preparation and the applicable product specification.</p>

    <h2>Nominal size is not measured diameter</h2>
    <p>DN, NPS and regional A designations are nominal references. They must not be treated as direct measured outside diameter or inside diameter values.</p>

    <h2>Standards relationships require context</h2>
    <p>A related, adopted, modified or dimensionally similar standard is not automatically interchangeable. Edition, scope, dimensions, material, mechanical properties, test requirements, certification, regulation and intended use must be checked separately.</p>

    <h2>Source labels</h2>
    <p>HowNote separates official metadata, manufacturer cross-checks, regional aliases and calculated values. A manufacturer publication or a HowNote calculation is not presented as a substitute for the complete official standard.</p>

    <h2>Purchasing and compliance</h2>
    <p>Before ordering, confirm the product standard, dimension standard, edition/year, size, schedule or wall thickness, material grade, tolerances, testing, MTC/MTR requirements, marking, packing and destination-market compliance in the supplier confirmation and purchase order.</p>

    <h2>No warranty of suitability</h2>
    <p>HowNote does not guarantee that a product is suitable, compliant, certifiable or interchangeable for a particular application. The person or organization making the engineering, purchasing or compliance decision remains responsible for the final review.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
